pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test: `is_overflow_safe_leq` guarded `degree - 1` for the
% `... <== ... <= ...` branch, which stores `degree + 1`. At degree == i64::MAX
% the guard passed, the increment wrapped to i64::MIN and the forcing
% reification normalized into the trivially true `2^63 ~x1 >= 0` -- so this
% implication obligation was discharged against a row the proof never wrote.
% The correct constraint, `9223372036854775808 x1 >= 9223372036854775808`, is
% not implied by `1 x1 1 x2 >= 1`.
f 1 ;
ia x1 <== <= 9223372036854775807 : 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
